# ESLint across the TypeScript packages and the e2e suite, and Ruff across the
# Python package. `lint` fans out to all of it: nx runs the `eslint` target on
# each TypeScript package and the `lint` target (ruff) on threat-composer-ai,
# and the root script adds e2e, which is a standalone package rather than a
# workspace and so is not reachable through the workspace filter.
#
# This is exactly what CI runs, so the hook and CI cannot drift.
#
# Note the two halves behave differently, as they did before this change. The
# per-package eslint scripts pass --fix, so TypeScript problems are corrected
# in place -- and because that happens after staging, the fixes are NOT in the
# commit; re-stage and amend if it edits anything. Ruff is check-only; fix
# Python with
# `cd packages/threat-composer-ai && uv run ruff check . --fix && uv run ruff format .`
pnpm lint
